The describe_data_view returned a JSON string; need to parse. It shows time_field is "timestamp". Also fields include many.

So TIME_FIELD: timestamp

Now step 2: create dashboard.

We need to construct panels specs.

Panel 1 spec:

- title: maybe "Requests over time" (any human readable). Must be minLength 1.
- chart_type: "line"
- data_view: "Kibana Sample Data Logs"
- metrics: array with one object: agg "count", field null, label "requests". Ensure required fields: agg present.

We also might need to specify time_field? Not in panel spec; the data view's time_field is auto. So fine.

Panel 2 spec:

- title: "Requests by response code"
- chart_type: "bar" (or "column"? but bar allowed)
- data_view: same
- metrics: count agg, field null, label maybe "requests".
- group_by: array with one item: field "response.code", kind "terms", limit 10. Need to ensure field name correct. In fields list we saw "response":"string","response.keyword":"string". So field likely "response.code"? Actually the field for HTTP response code is probably "response.code". Let's verify typical structure: In Apache logs, field "response" may hold status code as string; there might be "response.code". The field list includes "response": string, "response.keyword": string. Not sure about "response.code". Could be nested? Usually it's just "response". Might be "response". Let's assume the field is "response". But to be safe, maybe use "response" as field for grouping.

But the requirement: number of requests by HTTP response code. So we need to group by the response code field. Which field holds the code? In sample data logs, there is a field "response" (string). Possibly contains status code like "200". There's also "response.keyword". I'd guess just "response". Let's use "response".

So group_by: [{"field":"response","kind":"terms","limit":10}].

Now we need to create dashboard with these two panels.

We must call create_dashboard. Parameters:

- title: 'LOC-fdb62b5b Web logs'
- space: default (maybe same as data view; not needed)
- panels: array of panel specs (each is object with required fields). Ensure each spec includes title, chart_type, data_view, metrics. Also group_by for second.

Check that create_dashboard expects "panels" items to have properties: title, chart_type, data_view, metrics, plus optional description, time_range, space, etc. The spec in tool says:

type create_dashboard = (_: {
// Title
title: string,
// Panels (array)
panels: // PanelSpec[]
{
    },
// Description
description?: string,
// Time range
time_range?: // Date math or ISO start and end.
{
    from?: string; // default: now-7d
    to?: string;   // default: now
},
// Space
space?: string, // default: null (default space)
}) => any;

Panel spec shape: from the tool description earlier for create_dashboard panels:

"panels": {
    "title": string,
    "chart_type": enum,
    "data_view": string,
    "time_field": string|null,
    "metrics": metrics[],
    "group_by": array of group_by objects,
    "filters": filters[]
}

But the detailed schema for panel in create_dashboard: In tool description, PanelSpec has fields:

{
 // Human-readable chart title.
 title: string,
 // Chart to draw...
 chart_type: enum,
 // Data view name...
 data_view: string,
 // Time field of the data view. Auto-filled if omitted.
 time_field?: string | null,
 // What to measure (1+).
 metrics: Metric[]
 // How to split the data...
 group_by: GroupBy[]
 // Optional equality filters ANDed together.
 filters: Filter[]
}

We need to ensure we include required fields: title, chart_type, data_view, metrics. Others optional.

Now construct panel specs.

Panel 1:

{
 "title": "Requests over time",
 "chart_type": "line",
 "data_view": "Kibana Sample Data Logs",
 "metrics": [
   {
     "agg": "count",
     "field": null,
     "label": "requests"
   }
 ],
 // No group_by needed; we can omit.
}

Panel 2:

{
 "title": "Requests by response code",
 "chart_type": "bar",
 "data_view": "Kibana Sample Data Logs",
 "metrics": [
   {
     "agg": "count",
     "field": null,
     "label": "requests"
   }
 ],
 "group_by": [
   {
     "field": "response",
     "kind": "terms",
     "limit": 10
   }
 ]
}

Check that "field" type is string; response is string.

Now call create_dashboard with title and panels.

Potential issue: The data_view name must match exactly the data view name. In describe_data_view we got name "Kibana Sample Data Logs". That's the display name, not the index pattern. But likely acceptable as data_view parameter (string). We'll use that exact string.

Now execute create_dashboard.
